outputs.L2:
A diesel fuel formulation that includes:

1. a first additive (i), which contains a quaternary ammonium salt; and  
2. a second additive (ii), which contains a Mannich reaction product;

where the quaternary ammonium salt additive (i) is obtained by reacting a non-ester quaternising agent with a compound produced from the reaction of a hydrocarbyl-substituted acylating agent and an amine represented by formula (B1) or (B2). In these formulae, R2 and R3 may be identical or different and are alkyl, alkenyl, or aryl groups containing 1 to 22 carbon atoms; X represents either a direct bond or an alkylene group containing 1 to 20 carbon atoms; n has a value from 0 to 20; m has a value from 1 to 5; and R4 is either hydrogen or a C1 to C22 alkyl group.

The Mannich reaction product additive (ii) is produced through a Mannich reaction involving:  
(d) an aldehyde;  
(e) an amine; and  
(f) a substituted phenol;  

where the substituted phenol bears at least one branched hydrocarbyl substituent having a molecular weight in the range of 200 to 3000.

counterfactuals.output:
1. **A diesel fuel composition** comprising a major amount of a diesel fuel and a minor amount of a detergent additive combination, the detergent additive combination comprising:

   (a) a quaternary ammonium salt detergent obtained by quaternising a reaction product of:  
   (i) an acylating agent comprising a hydrocarbyl-substituted acylating agent; and  
   (ii) an amine comprising at least one tertiary amino group;  
   with a quaternising agent that is not an ester; and

   (b) a Mannich detergent obtained by reacting:  
   (i) an aldehyde;  
   (ii) an amine; and  
   (iii) a phenol substituted with a branched hydrocarbyl group;

   wherein the quaternary ammonium salt detergent and the Mannich detergent are present in amounts effective to improve detergency of the diesel fuel composition.
